WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.860
Terraform state is operationally sensitive.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:15.640
It maps configuration to real infrastructure and can include resource identifiers, dependency relationships, outputs, metadata, configuration details, and secret-adjacent values.

3
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:22.540
Even when sensitive values are marked carefully, state can still reveal how an environment is structured and which resources matter.

4
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.000
A helper script should treat state as a protected artifact, not as ordinary temporary output.

5
00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.040
Backend protection is central to safe Terraform automation.

6
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:41.340
Remote state backends should have appropriate access control, encryption where applicable, locking, versioning, audit logs, and ownership.

7
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:47.200
Helper scripts should confirm that the expected backend is in use before planning or applying.

8
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:56.660
If backend initialization fails, state locking fails, or the backend does not match the expected environment, the script should stop rather than continue with uncertain state.

9
00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:02.460
Local state, plan files, and generated output files also need careful handling.

10
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:11.440
They should not be left casually in shared directories, uploaded as broad CI/CD artifacts, committed to repositories, or printed into logs.

11
00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:17.540
Plan files can contain sensitive details and can become stale if the environment changes after review.

12
00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:24.520
Outputs may include identifiers, endpoints, policy names, or other details that help explain the environment.

13
00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:28.540
Helper scripts should keep retention and access rules clear.

14
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.900
Logging should support operations without spreading sensitive data.

15
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:40.920
It is useful to record the environment, workspace, backend category, action, result, and relevant high-level status.

16
00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:49.900
It is usually not useful to dump large portions of state, raw plan details, sensitive outputs, provider credentials, or environment variables into logs.

17
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:57.840
Secure Terraform helper scripts protect state, handle artifacts deliberately, and fail safely when state protections are not available.
